 "assumptions": {
  "connector formation": "Ke = B^T K B with B = Q^T[-I, S(a_i)+S(r)/2, I, -S(a_j)+S(r)/2] on translations and Q^T[0, -I, 0, I] on rotations, S(v)w = v x w, r = (x_j - x_i) + (a_j - a_i); K = D^-1 H D^-1, D = diag(Ls, Ls, Ls, 1, 1, 1); each entry one exact sum rounded once (core/solver/frame_kernel/src/connector.rs module comment and b(), global_stiffness(), decode_work_matrix()). Checked here: every entry of B, K and Ke is exact in binary64, so the product's formed and intended systems are this exact system.",
  "replaced span": "the replaced pipe A-B contributes no stiffness, self-weight or load (execution/PKG-03/DEL-03-06/ScopeOfWork.md, Replaced span; AC-004). No case here has self-weight or thermal load.",
  "free system": "node A anchored on all six DOFs with zero prescribed motion; the free DOFs are B's six in the order UX, UY, UZ, RX, RY, RZ; an active stop makes B's UZ a prescribed row at its ground 0.",
  "scaling": "row exponent e_i = -floor(floor(log2 K_ii) / 2), K_s = D K D with D = diag(2^e_i) (core/solver/frame_kernel/src/structural.rs prepare_bound and binary_exponent); an even force scale 2^b shifts every e_i by -b/2 and leaves K_s unchanged (structural.rs unscale_structural_solution comment).",
  "estimator": "Hager iteration from x = e/n, at most five passes, stopping on no increase, on |z_j| <= z.x or a repeated index (ties: the last maximal index), then the alternating vector (-1)^i (1 + i/(n-1)) scaled by 2/(3n); est = the larger (structural.rs ConditionMatrix::estimate_condition). The replay below is in exact arithmetic; the product's is binary64.",
  "premise": "Lambda = 1024 est / (1 - 1024 est eps_E), used as the bound on ||K_s^-1||_inf (core/solver/frame_kernel/src/structural/formation_check.rs, after the second correction).",
  "loads": "each load term enters the intended force exactly: a DOF's force is the exact sum of its terms (core/solver/frame_kernel/src/load_ledger.rs accumulate_dof).",
  "one-way law": "a stop bearing with a positive (negative) reaction is admissible active when its reaction K u - f at its DOF is > 0 (< 0), and admissible inactive when its displacement is > 0 (< 0) with ground 0 (core/solver/nonlinear_integration/src/confirmation.rs support_reason; execution/PKG-04/DEL-04-04/ScopeOfWork.md one-way law)."
